          "snippet": "However, the same PDE can be tied to different SDEs depending on the stochastic integration scheme, e.g., Ito, Stratonovich (Risken, 1996;Oksendal, 2003), Hanggi (Hänggi, 1978), α-type etc. An \"A-type\" interpretation is one such scheme (Ao et al, 2007;Shi et al, 2012). It is widely used in non-equilibrium studies in physics and biology (Wang et al, 2008;Zhu et al, 2004) because it allows one to compute the steady-state distribution easily; its implications are supported by other mathematical analyses such as Tel et al (1989); Qian (2014).",
